    <!--
      Character-forge BFF schema. Liquibase runs over a JDBC datasource (Liquibase
      has no R2DBC runner); all runtime data access goes through R2DBC.

        001 — character_forge_character (uuid PK DB-generated via gen_random_uuid;
              owner_subject = the IMMUTABLE Casdoor sub, NEVER localpart; per-brand
              `domain` column following the forum-bff 003 treatment; jsonb
              `definition` holding the canonical, fully server-validated Char3DConfig;
              `active` + the PARTIAL UNIQUE index enforcing ONE active character per
              (owner_subject, domain))

      POSTGRES-ONLY BY DESIGN: jsonb, gen_random_uuid() and the partial unique index
      are Postgres features. The test store IS Postgres (Testcontainers via the
      commons PostgresTestSupport + PostgresSliceTestConfig — the forum-bff 004
      precedent that moved slices off H2), and the production runtime is Postgres.
    -->

    <include file="db/changelog/001-character-forge-character.xml"/>
